<ecore:EPackage xmi:version="2.0" xmlns:xmi="http://www.omg.org/XMI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:ecore="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore" name="server" nsURI="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:xml-analysis:rowset:server"
    nsPrefix="rssrv">
  <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
    <details key="documentation" value="The DISCOVER_* rowsets: what a server says about itself and about the protocol - its connections, locks, sessions, memory and traces, and the six XMLA 1.1 defines itself, among them DISCOVER_SCHEMA_ROWSETS, by which a server states what else it can be asked.&#xA;&#xA;The nsURI of this package was chosen by this project and is not specified by anyone. [MS-SSAS] and XMLA 1.1 give all rowsets one single namespace, urn:schemas-microsoft-com:xml-analysis:rowset, and a server states it once per response - one recorded session carries 19 inline schemas that all declare it. XSD allows many schema documents to share a target namespace; an EMF EPackage cannot, so more than one rowset package can never carry the specified value and every one of them needs an identifier of its own. This one is shaped like a Microsoft namespace so that the family stays visible, but Microsoft did not issue it. The specified namespace is where it belongs: on every feature, literally, and in XmlaNamespaces.ROWSET.&#xA;&#xA;Generated by spec/split_rowset_packages.py.&#xA;&#xA;The Restrictions classes here are the deliberate exception to everything above. They are API objects for clients and connectors and are never serialized - nothing writes a Restrictions object to a wire. Their features therefore resolve ##targetNamespace to this package, which means nothing, and the test that every rowset column names the rowset namespace skips them for that reason. Their feature order is the order the RestrictionsMask bitmask is defined over, and a restriction's name on the wire is its ExtendedMetaData name.&#xA;&#xA;They are in this package rather than beside it so that a rowset and what may restrict it cannot be loaded apart: they were separate once, half of them was staged in a test, and the server answered that a restriction it models was not recognized."/>
    <details key="oSGiCompatible" value="true"/>
    <details key="basePackage" value="org.eclipse.daanse.xmla.model.rowset"/>
    <details key="prefix" value="RowsetServer"/>
    <details key="fileExtensions" value="xmlarsrssrv"/>
    <details key="resource" value="XML"/>
    <details key="literalsInterface" value="true"/>
  </eAnnotations>
